Description:

A malformed If: header on a DAV request no longer crashes the httpd worker.
Two unparseable forms -- a tagged-list token with no closing ">", and an If
header with no condition list at all -- led to a NULL dereference that any
authenticated DAV client could trigger.

Tracked as GitHub security advisory GHSA-mhq5-r6qx-pwvg.


